# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo holds the CODE only. Two categories are deliberately excluded:
#
#  1. Media (758MB of source audio and generated frames) -- regenerable output
#     or user-owned masters.
#  2. The album/song directories. Their storyboard .json/.md embed full song
#     lyrics for unreleased tracks. grok.py can use one as a few-shot template
#     via STUDIO_TEMPLATE_JSON / STUDIO_TEMPLATE_MD pointing at a local path;
#     it falls back to a built-in placeholder exemplar when absent, so a clean
#     clone still runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Album / song working directories (lyrics, storyboards, renders)
/Street Cats/
/Catatonic/
/Get Feral Tonight/
/Nine Lives After Dark/
/reroll/
/anchor_v2/
/anchor_v3/
/anchor_v4/
# A model comparison sweep, 16 MB of renders. Regenerable output by the rule at
# the top of this file: the harness and the exact prompt that produced it are
# what matter, and they are written up in the day-8 continuation.
/zimage_sweep/

# Media
*.mp3
*.wav
*.flac
*.mp4
*.mov
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.pdf
*.zip

# Studio runtime state: sqlite db, uploads, job logs, generated output
studio/data/
studio/venv/

# Credentials -- never commit, wherever they land
*.env
!*.env.example
grok-mcp.env

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store

# Agent / session scratch state
.omc/
CONTINUATION-*.md

# Session scratch and unreleased track names -- not code
prompt.txt
MeowP_Albums_Track_Lists.md
